  "tactics": {
    "styleTags": [
      "Defensive Solidity",
      "Physical",
      "Counter-Attack",
      "Hard to Beat"
    ],
    "tacticalNote": "Alfaro organizes Paraguay in a deep 4-2-3-1 with two holding midfielders sitting narrowly in front of the back four, eliminating central spaces. They defend in two disciplined banks before launching rapid counter-attacks through Almir\u00f3n's movement on the right and Enciso's creativity centrally. Set pieces \u2014 both offensive and defensive \u2014 are meticulously prepared and represent their most reliable route to goals against elite opposition.",
    "strength": "Defensive compactness that suffocates space \u2014 even top-10 sides have historically found it extremely difficult to break down a well-organized Paraguay.",
    "vulnerability": "Sustained possession pressure from multiple angles can stretch the defensive structure, and when forced to chase a deficit they lack the individual quality to dominate open games."
  },
  "watchFor": [
    "Enciso's movement between the lines \u2014 when he finds pockets behind the USA midfield, Paraguay are at their most dangerous",
    "The defensive block in the first 60 minutes \u2014 Paraguay's strategy is to absorb and frustrate before striking late",
    "Set piece routines \u2014 both defending and attacking corners are central to Paraguay's game plan"
  ],
